# p_8b2f — Weekend Armchair: Remote and Blanket Leave the Couch

On weekends the living room furniture is used differently. The remote_shared is on the coffee_table_l1 even at 03:00 (×1), at 20:00 (×4), and at 21:00 (×1, with one outlier at tv_stand_l1). It never returns to the TV stand during the weekend; the residents watch TV in the afternoon and evening and leave the remote on the coffee table. On weekdays the remote is at tv_stand_l1 (03:00 ×3, 18:00 ×1), so this is a weekend-specific pattern.

The blanket_shared on weekends is on the armchair_l1 at 03:00 (×1), 18:00 (×1), and 20:00 (×1, with one at coffee_table_l1), then moves to coffee_table_l1 at 21:00 (×1) and 22:00 (×1). On weekdays the blanket is on the couch all day. The armchair is Priya's weekend reading chair; she drapes the blanket over it in the morning and afternoon, and it only migrates to the coffee table when the evening TV session begins.

What sets this apart: it is the only document that places the remote on the coffee table on weekends (not the TV stand) and the blanket on the armchair (not the couch). It differs from p_c9d4 and its forks which assume the weekday couch/TV-stand pattern applies to both day types. What would refute it: remote_shared at tv_stand_l1 at 20:00 on a Saturday, or blanket_shared at couch_l1 at 18:00 on a weekend day.

