# p_5d1a — Weekend Vacuum: Midday and Afternoon Floor Time (fork of p_d3f7)

This fork of p_d3f7 adds the weekend cleaning pattern that the parent ignores. The parent models two weekday windows (15:00 and 18:00) but gives the vacuum a single "both" base block at storage_floor_s1 with no weekend-specific floor time. The weekend evidence is clear: vacuum_cleaner_shared is on floor_l_l1 at 03:00 (×1), 12:00 (×1), 15:00 (×1), and 18:00 (×1, alongside storage ×2). On weekends the vacuum is out on the floor far more often than on weekdays, with a midday cleaning (12:00) that has no weekday equivalent.

The 03:00 weekend floor sighting (×1) suggests the vacuum is left out overnight after a Saturday afternoon clean. The 12:00 and 15:00 floor sightings indicate a two-window weekend cleaning: a midday pass (11:00–13:00) and an afternoon pass (14:00–16:00). The 18:00 split (floor ×1, storage ×2) means the evening is sometimes a third brief pass or the vacuum is being put away.

What changed from the parent: added weekend blocks for floor_l_l1 at 11:00–13:00 and 14:00–16:00 (both "sometimes"), and a weekend 03:00 floor block ("rarely" to capture the left-out-overnight case). The weekday blocks are unchanged. What would refute it: vacuum_cleaner_shared at storage_floor_s1 at 12:00 on a Saturday (no midday weekend cleaning), or at floor_l_l1 at 09:00 on multiple weekend days (the morning is also a weekend cleaning window).

